<title>COLOMBIA: Moderate quake shakes eastern Colombia.</title>
<headline>Moderate quake shakes eastern Colombia.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A moderate earthquake measuring 4.9 on the open-ended Richter scale shook an oil-producing area of eastern Colombia on Sunday, but there were no reports of damage, authorities said.</p>
<p>The epicenter of the quake, which struck at 8:20 a.m local time (1320 GMT), was in a jungle-region of Casanare province, a spokesman for the National Seismology Institute said.</p>
<p>Casanare is home to extensive oil operations run by British Petroleum Co Plc. Company officials were not available for comment on the earthquake.</p>
</text>
